Mouse,

The CMOS battery should be on the mainboard, but the mainboard is not 
the mainboard if that makes sense. The PCI and ISA slots are actually on 
a separate board from the CPU/RAM/CMOS battery. If you remove the 
clamshell portion of the case and look where the PS/2, parallel, etc 
ports are you should see two lift tabs on a case-length PCB, this will 
be where the battery lives. It'll come up and out easily, then you can 
just slot it back in. Sorry if I am being unclear, I have the same model 
but it is late here so words are a bit hard x)

Just in case, here's the service manual, 5-12 and onward is what you're 
looking for: 
https://theretroweb.com/motherboard/manual/b30wwsma-60841c95f009e303767433.pdf

